        "A locked-off medium shot of a plain grey room. A single warm floor lamp stands on the left side of the frame. In the centre of the room is a clear glass table.\n\nThree objects sit on the table in a row, left to right: a tall clear bottle half full of water, a small black box, and a green apple.\n\nA woman stands behind the table facing the camera. She holds a red mug in her left hand at chest height. Her right hand rests flat on the tabletop with the fingers spread apart.\n\nThe tabletop stays transparent and her legs are visible through the glass. Light from the lamp passes through the bottle and falls on the table surface.\n\nThe camera holds one fixed framing for the whole shot. She does not pick up any of the objects."
