      "title": "WINDOWED OBJECT TEST",
      "inputs": [],
      "outputs": [],
      "properties": {},
      "widgets_values": [
        "WINDOWED OBJECT PLACEMENT TEST\n\nDoes the semantic bridge hold a described background across window seams?\n\n192 frames at window 90 / overlap 39 = THREE windows, TWO seams.\n192 is a legal run (17*11+5) and divides by 3, so it is on the audio\nclock as well.\n\nRUN IT TWICE, same seed, changing only alpha:\n    alpha 0.0    the baseline — the node short-circuits to a passthrough\n    alpha 0.10   the treatment\n\nSCORE AT THREE TIMESTAMPS — first frame, middle, last frame. A single\nverdict on the whole clip cannot see drift across a seam, which is the\nentire measurement.\n\n    1  exactly three objects on the table\n    2  order left to right: bottle, black box, green apple\n    3  lamp still on the LEFT of frame\n    4  tabletop still transparent, legs visible through it\n    5  mug still in the same hand\n    6  other hand still flat on the table, fingers separated\n    7  light still passing through the bottle onto the table\n    8  she never picks anything up\n\nCount how many hold at all three timestamps. If the adapter does what\nthe hypothesis says, the 0.0 run drifts across the seams and the 0.10\nrun holds.\n\nWHY NO REFERENCES. Nothing on that card exists in a reference image, so\nreferences would add a second possible cause for every failure without\nmeasuring anything. In H3 28 they also made the prompt 3% of the\nconditioning; here it is 100%, so an effect on prompt tokens is at full\nstrength.\n\nONE STRING NODE feeds both the reference node and the bridge. If those\ntwo ever differ the span is computed from the wrong text and the wrong\ntokens are transformed — this makes that impossible.\n\nWHY NO LoRAs. This is a measurement graph. A character LoRA in a scene\nwith no character is a confound, and the turbo LoRA changes what step\ncount means. Sage attention IS here: it changes speed, not output.\n\nWHAT WE ALREADY KNOW, so it is not re-litigated: freenoise and\noverlap-linear were both measured null, so the drift is not a blending\nartifact. A reference image of the set and a room description with\ncountable features were both tried and the seams still shifted. This\ntests something different — not a better description, a better ENCODING\nof one.\n\nREAD THE BRIDGE INFO. At alpha 0 it now prints a passthrough line, so\nboth runs leave a trace in the log."
      ],
      "color": "#432",
      "bgcolor": "#653"
    }
